WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.232
This is the course directory

00:00:02.232 --> 00:00:04.505
for the On-Chain Operator Program.

00:00:04.505 --> 00:00:06.351
In this film you will learn how

00:00:06.351 --> 00:00:08.140
to find a lesson, read it, run

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:10.517
its calculator, and keep your place.

00:00:10.517 --> 00:00:11.856
The page works in your

00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:13.602
browser, even with no network.

00:00:14.902 --> 00:00:17.467
A long course is easy to get lost in.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.057
This page is the map.

00:00:19.057 --> 00:00:20.959
Search it, or walk the stages, and

00:00:20.959 --> 00:00:22.970
you land on the lesson, the picture,

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:25.307
the worksheet, and the calculator together.

00:00:26.607 --> 00:00:27.835
By the end you will be

00:00:27.835 --> 00:00:29.362
able to do four things.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:31.752
Search for a lesson number or a topic.

00:00:31.752 --> 00:00:34.247
Open the lesson and read the full text.

00:00:34.247 --> 00:00:35.852
Run the calculator under that

00:00:35.852 --> 00:00:37.597
lesson, and read the graph.

00:00:37.597 --> 00:00:39.062
Then mark it done, and fill

00:00:39.062 --> 00:00:41.102
the worksheet without leaving the page.

00:00:42.402 --> 00:00:44.648
Start with the search box, which looks

00:00:44.648 --> 00:00:48.116
through lessons, pictures, worksheets, and calculators.

00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:51.374
The bar under the title jumps to lessons, glossary,

00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:55.371
worksheets, pictures, calculators, or where the files live.

00:00:55.371 --> 00:00:56.971
The list on the left walks

00:00:56.971 --> 00:00:59.581
six stages, from Zero through Operator.

00:00:59.581 --> 00:01:01.328
The picture under the title is

00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:02.736
that same path, in order.

00:01:04.036 --> 00:01:06.644
If you downloaded the zip, unzip it and

00:01:06.644 --> 00:01:09.226
open the HTML file in your browser.

00:01:09.226 --> 00:01:10.891
Do not look for a website.

00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:12.278
The page runs from the

00:01:12.278 --> 00:01:14.326
file itself, with no network.

00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:15.837
Read the safety line at the

00:01:15.837 --> 00:01:17.701
top before you type anything.

00:01:17.701 --> 00:01:20.012
It says the page is educational only,

00:01:20.012 --> 00:01:21.714
and it will never ask for a

00:01:21.714 --> 00:01:22.991
seed phrase or a key.

00:01:24.291 --> 00:01:26.181
Here is the size of the map.

00:01:26.181 --> 00:01:27.506
6 stages.

00:01:27.506 --> 00:01:29.021
15 modules.

00:01:29.021 --> 00:01:32.131
122 lessons on this page.

00:01:32.131 --> 00:01:34.144
And 20 calculators, each tied to

00:01:34.144 --> 00:01:36.701
the lesson that teaches that formula.

00:01:36.701 --> 00:01:38.516
There are also 17 worksheets.

00:01:39.816 --> 00:01:42.311
Above the lesson list are three filters.

00:01:42.311 --> 00:01:46.121
All lessons is the full list of 122.

00:01:46.121 --> 00:01:48.845
Mastery starters is the 15 openers, one

00:01:48.845 --> 00:01:51.051
at the start of each module.

00:01:51.051 --> 00:01:54.086
Expert lessons is the 15 expert cuts.

00:01:54.086 --> 00:01:56.530
Type a search, and the page looks through

00:01:56.530 --> 00:02:00.486
the whole directory: lessons, worksheets, pictures, and calculators.

00:02:01.786 --> 00:02:04.749
Stage Zero is Crypto From Zero: a wallet, a

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:08.146
first buy, and a backup, using a small amount.

00:02:08.146 --> 00:02:11.801
Foundations covers safety habits, then trading on chain.

00:02:11.801 --> 00:02:16.311
Practitioner covers lending and leverage, yield, and infrastructure risk.

00:02:17.611 --> 00:02:20.574
Analyst is where you research a protocol before you

00:02:20.574 --> 00:02:23.381
use it, and learn to read activity on chain.

00:02:23.381 --> 00:02:26.403
Strategist is the written operating system: the

00:02:26.403 --> 00:02:28.780
library, the plan, and the hedge.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.609
Operator is where you run the book,

00:02:30.609 --> 00:02:32.235
the credit line, and the review.

00:02:33.535 --> 00:02:35.820
Here is one study session, in order.

00:02:35.820 --> 00:02:38.045
First, search, or pick the stage.

00:02:38.045 --> 00:02:39.437
Then open the lesson and

00:02:39.437 --> 00:02:40.850
read it on the page.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:42.086
If that lesson has a

00:02:42.086 --> 00:02:44.680
calculator, run the example underneath.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:47.305
The graph redraws from the numbers you type.

00:02:47.305 --> 00:02:48.943
Fill the worksheet while the lesson

00:02:48.943 --> 00:02:50.380
is still in front of you.

00:02:50.380 --> 00:02:52.825
Then follow the next-lesson link at the bottom.

00:02:54.125 --> 00:02:58.095
Open lesson 3.4, Borrowing strategies and looping.

00:02:58.095 --> 00:03:00.894
The full lesson is on the page: the objective,

00:03:00.894 --> 00:03:04.350
the explanation, the picture, and the worked example.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:05.257
You do not need a

00:03:05.257 --> 00:03:06.415
second file to read it.

00:03:07.715 --> 00:03:10.909
Under the lesson, the calculator is already filled with

00:03:10.909 --> 00:03:14.175
the lesson example, and the graph shows that result.

00:03:14.175 --> 00:03:16.675
Change the borrow rate to 6%, and the

00:03:16.675 --> 00:03:19.870
headline and the graph both drop below zero.

00:03:19.870 --> 00:03:22.167
Press Back to the lesson example, and the

00:03:22.167 --> 00:03:24.410
lesson numbers and the graph both return.

00:03:25.710 --> 00:03:27.715
Watch three things move together.

00:03:27.715 --> 00:03:29.150
You type one number.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.625
The headline states the result in words.

00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:33.893
The graph draws that same result, so you

00:03:33.893 --> 00:03:36.350
can see the shape, not only the figure.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.245
Back to the lesson example restores all three.

00:03:39.245 --> 00:03:40.917
The form in the calculators

00:03:40.917 --> 00:03:42.710
section is a second copy.

00:03:42.710 --> 00:03:43.704
It does not share what

00:03:43.704 --> 00:03:44.870
you typed under the lesson.

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:48.765
Read the example the way the lesson does.

00:03:48.765 --> 00:03:52.340
Borrow LTV is 0.70.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:53.825
There are 3 loops.

00:03:53.825 --> 00:03:57.538
Collateral APY is 3.5%.

00:03:57.538 --> 00:04:00.893
Borrow APY is 2.5%.

00:04:00.893 --> 00:04:06.050
The page prints about 2.53× leverage, a net of

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:11.398
5.03%, and a breakeven borrow rate near 5.78%.

00:04:11.398 --> 00:04:13.643
These are lesson numbers, for learning.

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:15.298
They are not a forecast, and

00:04:15.298 --> 00:04:17.068
nothing here promises a result.

00:04:18.368 --> 00:04:19.578
Question one.

00:04:19.578 --> 00:04:22.853
The lesson example borrows at 2.5%.

00:04:22.853 --> 00:04:27.735
The calculator names a breakeven borrow rate near 5.78%.

00:04:27.735 --> 00:04:29.110
What happens at that rate?

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:36.540
The answer: the extra return is wiped out.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:38.375
The spread was the whole gain.

00:04:38.375 --> 00:04:40.790
This is a lesson example, not a forecast.

00:04:42.090 --> 00:04:44.180
Tick the box to mark the lesson done,

00:04:44.180 --> 00:04:46.790
and that check stays in this browser only.

00:04:46.790 --> 00:04:49.687
Search health factor, read the marked line,

00:04:49.687 --> 00:04:52.320
and open lesson 3.2 with its calculator.

00:04:53.620 --> 00:04:56.175
Four searches are enough to learn the page.

00:04:56.175 --> 00:04:59.760
Type 3.2, and the health factor lesson opens.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:02.078
Type health factor, and the matching line

00:05:02.078 --> 00:05:04.640
is marked, with the calculator beside it.

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:06.995
Type worksheet, and the sheets come up.

00:05:06.995 --> 00:05:10.665
Type 8.3, and the strategy library opens.

00:05:10.665 --> 00:05:11.919
A lesson number is the

00:05:11.919 --> 00:05:13.390
fastest search on the page.

00:05:14.690 --> 00:05:17.004
The glossary is the word list from

00:05:17.004 --> 00:05:19.451
lesson 0.8, and each word links back

00:05:19.451 --> 00:05:21.735
to the lesson that defines it.

00:05:21.735 --> 00:05:24.062
Worksheets are fillable on the page, what

00:05:24.062 --> 00:05:26.057
you type stays in this browser, and

00:05:26.057 --> 00:05:27.885
every secret stays off the sheet.

00:05:29.185 --> 00:05:32.827
Lesson 8.3 folds 30 strategies into levels, so

00:05:32.827 --> 00:05:35.375
you open one level at a time.

00:05:35.375 --> 00:05:38.664
Open Level 1 for the core set: stablecoin lending,

00:05:38.664 --> 00:05:43.114
staking, and borrowing against collateral, with illustrative numbers.

00:05:44.414 --> 00:05:46.539
Read a strategy in three moves.

00:05:46.539 --> 00:05:49.384
Open a single level, not the whole library.

00:05:49.384 --> 00:05:51.439
Name where the return comes from.

00:05:51.439 --> 00:05:54.114
Then read how that strategy loses money.

00:05:54.114 --> 00:05:57.404
If you cannot explain the unwind, leave it folded.

00:05:57.404 --> 00:05:59.638
The library says the same thing in its

00:05:59.638 --> 00:06:01.930
own line: if you cannot name the source

00:06:01.930 --> 00:06:03.649
and the way out, do not enter.

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:07.398
Pictures are grouped by module, and each

00:06:07.398 --> 00:06:09.669
diagram links back to its lesson.

00:06:09.669 --> 00:06:14.026
The health calculator draws the lesson example:

00:06:14.026 --> 00:06:18.020
10 at $3,000, threshold 0.80, debt $12,000,

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.014
health factor 2.00, liquidation near $1,500.

00:06:23.314 --> 00:06:24.815
Say the health factor out

00:06:24.815 --> 00:06:26.789
loud from the lesson example.

00:06:26.789 --> 00:06:31.649
10 units at $3,000 is $30,000 of collateral.

00:06:31.649 --> 00:06:36.589
Times a liquidation threshold of 0.80 is $24,000.

00:06:36.589 --> 00:06:39.018
Divided by $12,000 of debt,

00:06:39.018 --> 00:06:41.574
the health factor is 2.00.

00:06:41.574 --> 00:06:46.318
Liquidation sits near $1,500, about half the price.

00:06:46.318 --> 00:06:48.073
The graph shows that buffer.

00:06:48.073 --> 00:06:50.763
It is the lesson example, not a price target.

00:06:52.063 --> 00:06:54.912
Where things live names this directory as the map,

00:06:54.912 --> 00:06:57.314
and points to the Course Hub beside it for

00:06:57.314 --> 00:06:59.493
the video, the checklist, and the quiz.

00:07:00.793 --> 00:07:02.668
Split the folder in your mind.

00:07:02.668 --> 00:07:05.631
Inside this file you already have the lessons,

00:07:05.631 --> 00:07:08.973
the pictures, the 17 worksheets, the 20 calculators,

00:07:08.973 --> 00:07:11.543
search, the glossary, and mark done.

00:07:11.543 --> 00:07:14.029
Beside this file, in the course folder, you

00:07:14.029 --> 00:07:16.516
have the lesson videos, the Course Hub, the

00:07:16.516 --> 00:07:18.963
program book, and the Day-1 Setup Kit.

00:07:18.963 --> 00:07:21.125
If a video link does nothing, you are

00:07:21.125 --> 00:07:23.303
in the directory file on its own.

00:07:23.303 --> 00:07:25.168
Open the course folder for the film.

00:07:26.468 --> 00:07:27.713
Question two.

00:07:27.713 --> 00:07:30.398
You opened only the downloaded directory.

00:07:30.398 --> 00:07:32.403
A lesson video does not play.

00:07:32.403 --> 00:07:33.453
Where is the video?

00:07:37.873 --> 00:07:39.270
The answer: in the course

00:07:39.270 --> 00:07:40.968
folder, next to this file.

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:43.736
The directory zip keeps the page, not the films.

00:07:45.036 --> 00:07:46.106
Your turn.

00:07:46.106 --> 00:07:47.911
Open the directory file.

00:07:47.911 --> 00:07:49.516
Search 3.2.

00:07:49.516 --> 00:07:53.189
Open the lesson, run the health calculator, and confirm

00:07:53.189 --> 00:07:56.506
a health factor of 2.00 on the lesson example.

00:07:56.506 --> 00:07:58.221
Then mark the lesson done.

00:07:58.221 --> 00:08:00.776
Do not type a seed phrase, a private

00:08:00.776 --> 00:08:03.216
key, an API key, or a password.

00:08:03.216 --> 00:08:05.301
This program will not ask for them.

00:08:05.301 --> 00:08:07.596
The page is educational only.

00:08:07.596 --> 00:08:10.583
It is not financial, tax, or legal advice.

00:08:11.883 --> 00:08:13.128
Let's recap.

00:08:13.128 --> 00:08:15.293
Search, or walk the six stages.

00:08:15.293 --> 00:08:17.952
Read the lesson, then run its calculator, and

00:08:17.952 --> 00:08:20.448
treat the graph as the lesson example.

00:08:20.448 --> 00:08:23.393
Mark done, and fill the sheet, in this browser.

00:08:23.393 --> 00:08:25.967
Next, open lesson 0.0 if you are

00:08:25.967 --> 00:08:28.384
new, or lesson 3.2 if you want

00:08:28.384 --> 00:08:30.958
the health factor worked in full.
